# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
build/

# uv
# (uv.lock IS committed; the virtualenv is not)
.venv/
venv/

# Test / type / lint caches
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.dmypy.json
dmypy.json
.coverage
.coverage.*
coverage.xml
htmlcov/

# Live audit-pack output (a curated SAMPLE pack is committed under docs/audit-pack/ instead)
/dist/
/README.pdf

# Node (mermaid-cli is fetched on demand via npx; nothing is vendored)
node_modules/
package-lock.json

# Secrets / local config (SECURITY.md: there are no credentials in this repository, keep it so)
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key

# Logs and merge/patch leftovers
*.log
*.orig
*.rej

# Editors / OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# NOTE: `evidence/` (generated by `make seed-demo-data`) IS committed on purpose, and so are the
# rendered diagram PNG/SVGs under docs/diagrams/rendered/ -- the README must render on GitHub
# without a build step, and the committed evidence is part of the demonstrated audit trail.
# The same goes for docs/screenshots/, the sample pack under docs/audit-pack/ (incl. its PDF),
# uv.lock and .python-version. CI's determinism job also diffs `evidence/`, so never ignore it.
# Hence: no blanket `*.pdf`, `*.png`, `*.svg` or `*.json` rules above.
